WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.269 --> 00:00:02.353
- My next guest knows all too well

00:00:02.353 --> 00:00:04.939
what it's like to work
for the Royal household.

00:00:04.939 --> 00:00:07.535
He's the former royal butler
to His Royal Highness,

00:00:07.535 --> 00:00:10.352
Prince Charles and Camilla
the Duchess of Cornwall.

00:00:10.352 --> 00:00:12.934
Please welcome Mr. Grant Harold, y'all.

00:00:12.934 --> 00:00:13.767
(applause)

00:00:13.767 --> 00:00:16.245
- [Kelly] I mean, what was it like

00:00:16.245 --> 00:00:18.634
when you first met Prince
Charles and Camilla?

00:00:18.634 --> 00:00:20.801
- It was, it was, quite nerve-wracking

00:00:20.801 --> 00:00:23.978
in fact, I wasn't sure what
the, what the protocol was,

00:00:23.978 --> 00:00:25.797
what you're supposed to do,
what you're not supposed to do.

00:00:25.797 --> 00:00:28.685
And the confession I have to make

00:00:28.685 --> 00:00:29.918
is that I was in Scotland,

00:00:29.918 --> 00:00:31.856
there's this long corridor,

00:00:31.856 --> 00:00:34.368
and they appeared at the end
of the corridor and I panicked.

00:00:34.368 --> 00:00:36.506
And I remember thinking, what do you do?

00:00:36.506 --> 00:00:39.921
Can you speak to them? Can
you, do you not speak to them?

00:00:39.921 --> 00:00:40.764
(laughter)

00:00:40.764 --> 00:00:42.610
And there was a, there was a
door on the right hand side,

00:00:42.610 --> 00:00:43.966
so I thought, I'll went in that room,

00:00:43.966 --> 00:00:46.570
and I'll keep away for a minute
or two until they go past.

00:00:46.570 --> 00:00:50.534
Unfortunately, it wasn't a
room, it was a storage cupboard.

00:00:50.534 --> 00:00:51.440
(laughter)

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:53.958
- Did they think you were nuts?

00:00:53.958 --> 00:00:55.866
- [Grant] Yes. They did.

00:00:55.866 --> 00:00:56.699
(laughter)

00:00:56.699 --> 00:00:58.999
- [Grant] Because, there was
actually glass and bottles

00:00:58.999 --> 00:01:00.823
and so I thought, they're
gonna think I'm an, uh, uh..

00:01:00.823 --> 00:01:01.951
- [Kelly] ...alcoholic!

00:01:01.951 --> 00:01:03.136
- [Grant] ...alcoholic! Yeah, exactly.

00:01:03.136 --> 00:01:05.055
And I kinda stood there
and the next thing I heard

00:01:05.055 --> 00:01:07.490
was the Prince going, oh,
do you think he's okay?

00:01:07.490 --> 00:01:08.839
(laughter)

00:01:08.839 --> 00:01:09.672
- [Kelly] (gasps)

00:01:09.672 --> 00:01:12.602
- [Grant] And, I thought,
right, I better walk out.

00:01:12.602 --> 00:01:13.608
- [Kelly] (laughs)

00:01:13.608 --> 00:01:15.599
- [Grant] So I opened the
door and I tried to be

00:01:15.599 --> 00:01:17.710
very professional and I
didn't make eye contact

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:19.557
and there was a door on the other side,

00:01:19.557 --> 00:01:21.111
so I opened the door on the other side

00:01:21.111 --> 00:01:24.256
praying it wasn't another cupboard.

00:01:24.256 --> 00:01:26.552
And it was a staircase, and
I remember kind of going,

00:01:26.552 --> 00:01:27.915
ah, the staircase.

00:01:27.915 --> 00:01:29.633
And then they looked at me and went,

00:01:29.633 --> 00:01:30.767
good morning your Royal Highnesses.

00:01:30.767 --> 00:01:31.600
(laughter)

00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:32.955
And then carried on, and
luckily they started laughing.

00:01:32.955 --> 00:01:34.017
- [Kelly] Oh my gosh,

00:01:34.017 --> 00:01:34.850
(laughter)

00:01:34.850 --> 00:01:36.328
- [Kelly] That's amazing!

00:01:36.328 --> 00:01:37.519
(applause)

00:01:37.519 --> 00:01:39.109
All right well let's talk some tea, like,

00:01:39.109 --> 00:01:41.626
Hugh gave me a lot of crap, man.

00:01:41.626 --> 00:01:43.388
I'm just saying Grant, okay?

00:01:43.388 --> 00:01:44.986
But how did we do today?

00:01:44.986 --> 00:01:46.239
Silver? We have silver.

00:01:46.239 --> 00:01:47.296
- [Grant] So this is wonderful.

00:01:47.296 --> 00:01:48.600
- [Kelly] How have we done?

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:49.862
- [Grant] This is great, and you've got,

00:01:49.862 --> 00:01:50.810
is that a silver... is
that a silver teaspoon?

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:52.280
- [Kelly] Yeah, I will say though,

00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:54.298
I know that y'all don't like bags, right?

00:01:54.298 --> 00:01:55.546
You like loose leaf.

00:01:55.546 --> 00:01:56.573
'Cause I do too.

00:01:56.573 --> 00:01:57.969
- Well, bags are very, yeah, not

00:01:57.969 --> 00:01:58.802
(mumbles)

00:01:58.802 --> 00:02:00.359
- [Kelly] Okay. Posh, party of one.

00:02:00.359 --> 00:02:01.321
(laughter)

00:02:01.321 --> 00:02:03.556
- And you've got the lemon
which is, I've got to watch

00:02:03.556 --> 00:02:05.751
because I am sitting next
to country western royalty.

00:02:05.751 --> 00:02:06.848
- [Kelly] I know.

00:02:06.848 --> 00:02:08.710
- So I've got to kind of make sure I

00:02:08.710 --> 00:02:10.999
(background noise drowns out other sounds)

00:02:10.999 --> 00:02:12.610
(applause)

00:02:12.610 --> 00:02:13.443
Um, and we've got the lemon
so if it's an Earl Grey

00:02:13.443 --> 00:02:14.833
um, I assume this is Earl Grey tea.

00:02:14.833 --> 00:02:16.236
- [Kelly] I love Earl Grey.

00:02:16.236 --> 00:02:17.099
- [Grant] So, oh, fantastic.

00:02:17.099 --> 00:02:17.955
- [Kelly] Would you like to try it?

00:02:17.955 --> 00:02:18.875
- Oh, have you, have you...?

00:02:18.875 --> 00:02:20.752
- [Kelly] I've already - yeah,
I've... would you like to...

00:02:20.752 --> 00:02:21.770
I will take some more, sir.

00:02:21.770 --> 00:02:23.739
- Do you want me to - is
that okay? - we haven't got

00:02:23.739 --> 00:02:25.009
a tea strainer, have we? No.

00:02:25.009 --> 00:02:27.498
- [Kelly] I'm totally gonna
tell everyone that you, like,

00:02:27.498 --> 00:02:28.755
did this for royalty and then me.

00:02:28.755 --> 00:02:29.588
(laughter)

00:02:29.588 --> 00:02:31.477
- [Kelly] That makes me
so much cooler to myself.

00:02:31.477 --> 00:02:32.310
(laughter)

00:02:32.310 --> 00:02:34.371
- Oh, do you want some,
do you want some lemon?

00:02:34.371 --> 00:02:35.320
- [Kelly] No, I like it plain.

00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:36.283
- Okay, you're sure?

00:02:36.283 --> 00:02:38.043
- Oh no, yeah, lemon is great.

00:02:38.043 --> 00:02:38.899
(laughter)

00:02:38.899 --> 00:02:40.347
(background noise drowns out other sounds)

00:02:40.347 --> 00:02:42.493
- You don't have to do that, you don't!

00:02:42.493 --> 00:02:44.234
- [Kelly] Yes, I love lemon.

00:02:44.234 --> 00:02:45.067
- [Grant] You should love lemon

00:02:45.067 --> 00:02:45.900
(laughter)

00:02:45.900 --> 00:02:46.733
you should.

00:02:46.733 --> 00:02:47.566
- Love lemon.

00:02:47.566 --> 00:02:48.399
- Lovely.

00:02:48.399 --> 00:02:49.232
- Yeah. Maybe like, I
mean, let's just get sugar

00:02:49.232 --> 00:02:50.065
while we're at it. We're
growing, it's fine.

00:02:50.065 --> 00:02:50.898
- Sugar?

00:02:50.898 --> 00:02:51.731
- No?

00:02:51.731 --> 00:02:52.564
- No.

00:02:52.564 --> 00:02:53.397
- [Kelly] What?

00:02:53.397 --> 00:02:54.230
- You don't use sugar in Earl Grey.

00:02:54.230 --> 00:02:55.063
- [Kelly] No?

00:02:55.063 --> 00:02:55.896
- No it's...

00:02:55.896 --> 00:02:56.729
(scoffs)

00:02:56.729 --> 00:02:57.562
(laughter)

00:02:57.562 --> 00:02:58.395
- [Kelly] Why is it there?

00:02:58.395 --> 00:02:59.228
(laughter)

00:02:59.228 --> 00:03:00.061
- Wait, what?

00:03:00.061 --> 00:03:00.894
(applause)

00:03:00.894 --> 00:03:02.329
- [Grant] On this occasion I wouldn't.

00:03:02.329 --> 00:03:03.400
Not with, uh...

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:04.233
- No, me neither!

00:03:04.233 --> 00:03:05.196
I'm so steady.

00:03:05.196 --> 00:03:06.095
(laughter)

00:03:06.095 --> 00:03:07.699
- Yes, just one more little thing.

00:03:07.699 --> 00:03:10.199
Have you not got like a, um...

00:03:12.445 --> 00:03:13.278
- Oh! Yeah, there, okay.

00:03:13.278 --> 00:03:14.111
- No, no, no.

00:03:14.111 --> 00:03:15.414
- [Kelly] Er, no.

00:03:15.414 --> 00:03:16.247
(laughter)

00:03:16.247 --> 00:03:18.189
- Excuse me, excuse me.

00:03:18.189 --> 00:03:19.586
(applause)

00:03:19.586 --> 00:03:21.413
- I'm very fancy, Grant!

00:03:21.413 --> 00:03:23.540
- We need the saucer.

00:03:23.540 --> 00:03:25.340
- [Lesley] Oh yeah, the saucer!

00:03:25.340 --> 00:03:27.448
- [Kelly] Today I'm
bringing the class, Grant.

00:03:27.448 --> 00:03:28.709
- So... yes, I can tell, lovely

00:03:28.709 --> 00:03:31.609
(laughter)

00:03:31.609 --> 00:03:32.962
So, what we're gonna do, is,

00:03:32.962 --> 00:03:35.812
you're gonna do a very gentle
back and forward motion.

00:03:35.812 --> 00:03:38.037
And what you don't do

00:03:38.037 --> 00:03:38.870
(clinking)

00:03:38.870 --> 00:03:39.805
'cause we're not in a band or whatever.

00:03:39.805 --> 00:03:41.475
And then you place it on the side.

00:03:41.475 --> 00:03:42.416
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:03:42.416 --> 00:03:43.779
- [Grant] So, how would you do this bit?

00:03:43.779 --> 00:03:44.748
How would you pick it up?

00:03:44.748 --> 00:03:45.763
- Okay. How would I pick it up?

00:03:45.763 --> 00:03:47.182
- How would you pick the cup up?

00:03:47.182 --> 00:03:48.363
- Oh, well, by the tea thing?

00:03:48.363 --> 00:03:49.470
- Are you okay there?

00:03:49.470 --> 00:03:50.303
(laughter)

00:03:50.303 --> 00:03:51.224
- And then with a pinky?

00:03:51.224 --> 00:03:52.861
- I'm just like getting
ready to dance, Grant.

00:03:52.861 --> 00:03:53.917
(laughter)

00:03:53.917 --> 00:03:54.852
(applause)

00:03:54.852 --> 00:03:57.177
- This is how Americans do it.

00:03:57.177 --> 00:03:58.354
I just spilt it on myself.

00:03:58.354 --> 00:03:59.281
(applause)

00:03:59.281 --> 00:04:00.707
- No wait, what do you...

00:04:00.707 --> 00:04:01.641
- So you...

00:04:01.641 --> 00:04:02.474
- That was a workout!

00:04:02.474 --> 00:04:03.307
(laughter)

00:04:03.307 --> 00:04:05.357
- You might need...

00:04:05.357 --> 00:04:06.270
- Oh, sure.

00:04:06.270 --> 00:04:07.311
- So you can keep that.

00:04:07.311 --> 00:04:09.030
- I'm never gonna make
it as a royal, it's over.

00:04:09.030 --> 00:04:09.893
- No, it's fine.

00:04:09.893 --> 00:04:11.485
But I did notice you
kind of seem to kind of

00:04:11.485 --> 00:04:13.060
pick it up with two, um, hands.

00:04:13.060 --> 00:04:14.550
- Sometimes I do.

00:04:14.550 --> 00:04:15.992
- Just to reassure you, nobody's gonna

00:04:15.992 --> 00:04:17.038
steal it from you, dear.

00:04:17.038 --> 00:04:18.909
- You know what, you ain't
aware of where I'm from.

00:04:18.909 --> 00:04:19.742
(laughter)

00:04:19.742 --> 00:04:22.052
- Well, so, what you do is, you pick it up

00:04:22.052 --> 00:04:23.278
the whole thing together.

00:04:23.278 --> 00:04:24.213
- Okay.

00:04:24.213 --> 00:04:25.381
- And then we pick it up with the handle.

00:04:25.381 --> 00:04:26.214
We don't stick the pinkies out.

00:04:26.214 --> 00:04:27.120
We're not testing the wind direction.

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:28.206
- Are you even thirsty at this point?

00:04:28.206 --> 00:04:29.241
(laughter)

00:04:29.241 --> 00:04:30.280
- Isn't it exciting? It's riveting.

00:04:30.280 --> 00:04:31.694
- I've got my pinky.

00:04:31.694 --> 00:04:33.560
- No, no pinky's in, you're
not testing the wind direction.

00:04:33.560 --> 00:04:35.401
- Pinky in, pinky in.

00:04:35.401 --> 00:04:37.542
- We're not doing the weather forecast.

00:04:37.542 --> 00:04:38.375
- [Kelly] That's not a...

00:04:38.375 --> 00:04:39.605
- That's a myth, it's a myth. It's a myth.

00:04:39.605 --> 00:04:40.735
- [Grant] Absolutely, it's a myth.

00:04:40.735 --> 00:04:41.626
- Oh, totally.

00:04:41.626 --> 00:04:43.288
I just brought it up
so we could, you know,

00:04:43.288 --> 00:04:44.380
tell everybody it's a myth.

00:04:44.380 --> 00:04:45.263
- [Lesley] Yeah.

00:04:45.263 --> 00:04:46.113
(laughter)

00:04:46.113 --> 00:04:47.089
- [Grant] And then when we
drink, what we don't do,

00:04:47.089 --> 00:04:47.924
we don't go

00:04:47.924 --> 00:04:48.757
(slurps)

00:04:48.757 --> 00:04:49.590
- [Lesley] Well you don't do that.

00:04:49.590 --> 00:04:50.423
- [Kelly] Oh.

00:04:50.423 --> 00:04:51.256
- [Grant] We do it very, very...

00:04:51.256 --> 00:04:52.089
- No, we don't slurp.

00:04:52.089 --> 00:04:52.922
- [Grant] No, none of
that. So it's very gentle.

00:04:52.922 --> 00:04:53.755
- Like a lady.

00:04:53.755 --> 00:04:54.588
Are you doing it like a lady?

00:04:54.588 --> 00:04:56.210
- It's delicious.

00:04:56.210 --> 00:04:57.171
It's slightly cold.

00:04:57.171 --> 00:04:58.411
- [Kelly] It is.

00:04:58.411 --> 00:05:00.288
Well, it's been a minute.
The show's been on a minute.

00:05:00.288 --> 00:05:03.251
(laughter)

00:05:03.251 --> 00:05:04.587
- But it is delicious.

00:05:04.587 --> 00:05:06.028
So that's kind of how you, how you do it.

00:05:06.028 --> 00:05:07.261
And you'd have some sandwiches.

00:05:07.261 --> 00:05:09.316
I notice there were square sandwiches.

00:05:09.316 --> 00:05:10.185
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:05:10.185 --> 00:05:11.018
- Yes, that was lovely.

00:05:11.018 --> 00:05:13.293
- I am going to invite you to my barn

00:05:13.293 --> 00:05:14.820
and we're gonna have tea there.

00:05:14.820 --> 00:05:15.698
(laughter)

00:05:15.698 --> 00:05:16.531
- Your barn?

00:05:16.531 --> 00:05:17.364
- A barn.

00:05:19.443 --> 00:05:20.572
- Oh, can't wait.

00:05:20.572 --> 00:05:21.562
(laughter)

00:05:21.562 --> 00:05:23.066
- [Kelly] And then we're
gonna put you on a horse

00:05:23.066 --> 00:05:24.163
Western style!

00:05:24.163 --> 00:05:26.724
And then you're gonna go barrel
racing with Ms. McEntire.

00:05:26.724 --> 00:05:27.557
(laughter)

00:05:27.557 --> 00:05:29.135
- That I'd like to see!

